Q: Force narrowing conversion warning but avoid narrowing int-&gt;double conversion warning A: <p>I believe in your case the only solution the one that looks quite similar to yours in the end of question.</p>
<p>The only thing I would do, its using C++20 for having 2 separate constructors via concepts so it would be cleaner proposal</p>
<pre class="lang-cpp prettyprint-override"><code>template&lt;typename T&gt;
struct X {
    T v_;

    // Constructor A: For non-scalar types (like string_view)
    // We use () to allow standard conversions.
    template&lt;typename Other&gt;
    requires (!std::is_scalar_v&lt;T&gt;)
    X(Other&amp;&amp; v) : v_(std::forward&lt;Other&gt;(v)) {}

    // Constructor B: For scalar types (double, int, etc.)
    // We use {} to trigger the compiler's built-in narrowing check.
    template&lt;typename Other&gt;
    requires std::is_scalar_v&lt;T&gt;
    X(Other v) : v_{v} {} 
};
</code></pre>

